1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,935
Hello and welcome to the comprehensive project demonstration of the Bachat Gat Digital Savings Group Management System.

2
00:00:06,885 --> 00:00:17,595
A Bachat Gat, or Self-Help Group, is a vital community microfinance institution that empowers women and families in rural communities through collective thrift and mutual credit.

3
00:00:17,595 --> 00:00:24,576
Traditionally, self-help groups managed all contributions and loan accounts in handwritten physical paper ledgers.

4
00:00:24,576 --> 00:00:31,334
This frequently led to calculation errors, damaged books, lack of transparency, and delayed audits.

5
00:00:31,334 --> 00:00:38,305
To resolve these challenges permanently, we engineered this modern, robust, and fully digital web application.

6
00:00:38,305 --> 00:00:48,707
The platform provides centralized member management, monthly savings tracking, automated loan disbursement, interest accounting, repayments, and official financial registers.

7
00:00:48,707 --> 00:00:54,036
Let us begin by exploring the authentication system and role-based access control.

8
00:00:54,036 --> 00:01:03,972
To ensure financial integrity, the application strictly enforces role-based permissions, restricting administrative controls to verified group administrators.

9
00:01:03,972 --> 00:01:12,828
The admin login screen features clean, blank email and password inputs to respect user privacy and prevent unauthorized access.

10
00:01:12,828 --> 00:01:20,561
It provides a password visibility toggle as well as a secure self-service password reset flow via Firebase Authentication.

11
00:01:20,561 --> 00:01:26,483
Let us now log in using the verified administrator credentials and enter the live portal.

12
00:01:26,483 --> 00:01:31,716
Upon successful authentication, we arrive at the central executive Dashboard.

13
00:01:31,716 --> 00:01:39,703
The top header proudly displays the organization name, Chhatrapati Bachat Gat, Ghargaon Stand, alongside the Total Group Fund.

14
00:01:39,703 --> 00:01:46,091
Four core financial KPI cards provide instantaneous visibility into the group's financial health.

15
00:01:46,091 --> 00:01:53,432
The first card is Total Savings, representing eight thousand rupees in lifetime member contributions collected to date.

16
00:01:53,432 --> 00:02:00,752
The second card is Active Loans, reflecting four thousand rupees currently outstanding across active borrower accounts.

17
00:02:00,752 --> 00:02:07,309
The third card is Total Interest Earned, displaying the cumulative interest accrued from lending operations.

18
00:02:07,309 --> 00:02:14,703
The fourth card is Available Balance, showing four thousand rupees in liquid cash ready for fresh micro-loan disbursements.

19
00:02:14,703 --> 00:02:23,167
Here, Total Group Fund equals Total Savings plus Total Interest, and Available Balance equals Total Group Fund minus Active Loans.

20
00:02:23,167 --> 00:02:32,277
Below these cards, the Monthly Savings Target progress bar highlights the three lakh sixty-four thousand rupee goal, tracking paid versus pending members.

21
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:36,355
Next, let us navigate via the sidebar to Group Settings.

22
00:02:36,355 --> 00:02:42,044
This administrative console governs the foundational operating rules of the savings group.

23
00:02:42,044 --> 00:02:55,031
Here, the group name is established as Chhatrapati Bachat Gat, Ghargaon Stand, with a standard Monthly Contribution of one thousand rupees per share, and the Monthly Hafta Due Date set to the tenth of every month.

24
00:02:55,031 --> 00:03:03,760
Based on the three hundred and sixty-four registered members, the monthly group target of three lakh sixty-four thousand rupees is dynamically computed.

25
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:12,817
Any modification saved here instantly synchronizes across all calculations, dashboard metrics, and monthly financial reports in real time.

26
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:15,741
Let us now inspect the Members module.

27
00:03:15,741 --> 00:03:21,493
Chhatrapati Bachat Gat currently maintains three hundred and sixty-four registered community members.

28
00:03:21,493 --> 00:03:32,288
Crucially, all members are strictly sorted in ascending numerical order by their Member ID, progressing smoothly from M-one, M-two, all the way to M-three hundred and sixty-four.

29
00:03:32,288 --> 00:03:42,033
Administrators can toggle between All Members and Pending Dues tabs, or utilize the responsive search bar to locate members instantly by name or code.

30
00:03:42,033 --> 00:03:47,002
Opening an individual member profile reveals their complete financial ledger.

31
00:03:47,002 --> 00:03:57,595
Real phone numbers are displayed with the international plus ninety-one prefix, while members without a recorded phone number remain cleanly blank without confusing fake numbers.

32
00:03:57,595 --> 00:04:03,675
Add Member and Edit Member modals make member administration effortless and transparent.

33
00:04:03,796 --> 00:04:07,135
Now let us examine the Monthly Savings register.

34
00:04:07,085 --> 00:04:11,503
Regular thrift collection is the lifeblood of every self-help group.

35
00:04:11,503 --> 00:04:17,806
This module enables filtering by month and year to inspect contribution records across the group.

36
00:04:17,806 --> 00:04:25,962
The table displays member details, contribution amount, payment date, and payment mode, alongside the aggregate collection badge.

37
00:04:25,962 --> 00:04:36,534
When recording a contribution via the Record Savings action, administrators select the member and payment mode such as Cash, UPI, Bank Transfer, or Cheque.

38
00:04:36,534 --> 00:04:42,880
To eliminate accidental duplicate entries, the system features an explicit Double-Confirmation Modal.

39
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:51,693
The modal presents a clear confirmation prompt stating the exact month, year, and contribution amount, proceeding only when the user confirms.

40
00:04:51,693 --> 00:04:55,316
Next, we move to the Loans and Repayments module.

41
00:04:55,316 --> 00:05:00,920
Providing timely credit access to member entrepreneurs is a central mission of the Bachat Gat.

42
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:10,316
The module organizes loans into Active Loans and Closed Loans tabs, with summary metrics tracking total disbursed capital and outstanding principal.

43
00:05:10,316 --> 00:05:22,541
Clicking Issue Loan opens the loan issuance modal, where administrators select the borrowing member, enter the principal amount, tenure in months, and the standard monthly interest rate of two percent.

44
00:05:22,541 --> 00:05:33,854
The system performs real-time liquidity validation against available group funds and prompts the administrator with a Double-Confirmation dialog before disbursement, preventing erroneous transactions.

45
00:05:33,854 --> 00:05:37,329
Let us now examine the Loan Repayment workflow.

46
00:05:37,329 --> 00:05:48,261
Clicking Loan Repayment opens the repayment register, listing every member with an active loan, original borrowing amount, paid principal, remaining principal, and accrued interest.

47
00:05:48,261 --> 00:05:55,433
Selecting a loan launches the repayment drawer, which automatically computes the applicable monthly interest at two percent.

48
00:05:55,433 --> 00:06:03,695
Borrowers can make interest-only payments or contribute towards principal repayment, with the new outstanding balance updated dynamically.

49
00:06:03,695 --> 00:06:10,549
Submitting the payment triggers a Double-Confirmation Modal displaying the borrower name and exact repayment amount.

50
00:06:10,549 --> 00:06:18,876
Upon confirmation, the transaction is recorded, and loans reaching zero outstanding principal are automatically marked as CLOSED.

51
00:06:18,876 --> 00:06:23,473
Now let us explore the comprehensive Financial Reports and Registers.

52
00:06:23,473 --> 00:06:30,189
Transparent reporting is indispensable for group governance, annual general meetings, and statutory audits.

53
00:06:30,189 --> 00:06:44,479
The primary report is the Monthly Financial Register, displaying all three hundred and sixty-four members sorted numerically from M-one to M-three hundred and sixty-four, detailing savings, loans, interest, repayments, and net pending dues.

54
00:06:44,479 --> 00:06:51,672
The Pending Dues tab filters down to members with outstanding obligations, preserving exact numerical order.

55
00:06:51,672 --> 00:06:56,026
The Loans Overview tab provides an end-to-end loan book audit.

56
00:06:56,026 --> 00:07:04,787
Reports can be reviewed in printable view, sent directly to physical print, or exported as structured CSV files for spreadsheet accounting.

57
00:07:04,787 --> 00:07:10,032
Returning to the Dashboard, let us review the Recent Transactions and Activity feed.

58
00:07:10,032 --> 00:07:14,130
Clicking View All opens the comprehensive activity ledger modal.

59
00:07:14,130 --> 00:07:19,924
A standout feature here is the multi-category transaction filter, mirroring the mobile experience.

60
00:07:19,924 --> 00:07:30,751
Users can filter transactions across eight distinct categories: All, monthlyInvestment, loanIssue, loanRepayment, interestPayment, adjustment, otherIncome, and otherExpense.

61
00:07:30,751 --> 00:07:37,859
This targeted filtering allows auditors and administrators to isolate specific financial events instantly.

62
00:07:37,859 --> 00:07:44,013
Let us now review the underlying mathematical formulas and business invariants governing the platform.

63
00:07:44,013 --> 00:07:54,384
All figures are calculated dynamically from database collections using formal invariants: Monthly Target equals Total Active Members multiplied by Monthly Share.

64
00:07:54,384 --> 00:07:59,554
Total Group Fund equals Total Member Savings plus Total Cumulative Interest.

65
00:07:59,554 --> 00:08:04,501
Available Balance equals Total Group Fund minus Active Loans Outstanding.

66
00:08:04,501 --> 00:08:11,185
Monthly Interest equals Outstanding Principal multiplied by the monthly interest rate divided by one hundred.

67
00:08:11,185 --> 00:08:18,304
These strict invariants ensure that accounting remains mathematically consistent and audit-ready at all times.

68
00:08:18,412 --> 00:08:24,961
Now let us review the software architecture and technology stack verified directly from the project source.

69
00:08:24,911 --> 00:08:33,068
The client interface is built with React eighteen and bundled via Vite for lightning-fast responsiveness and modular code-splitting.

70
00:08:33,068 --> 00:08:40,790
The backend data store utilizes Google Firebase Firestore, providing real-time document synchronization across collections.

71
00:08:40,790 --> 00:08:46,585
Security is enforced through Firebase Authentication combined with role-based access rules.

72
00:08:46,585 --> 00:08:53,608
The application also features a dynamic internationalization context supporting both Marathi and English.

73
00:08:53,608 --> 00:09:00,155
The entire user interface is fully responsive across desktop, tablet, and mobile screens.

74
00:09:00,155 --> 00:09:09,244
In conclusion, the Chhatrapati Bachat Gat Management System is a complete, enterprise-grade digital platform designed for grassroots financial inclusion.

75
00:09:09,244 --> 00:09:20,695
By digitizing member profiles, savings collection, micro-loans, repayments, and audit-ready reporting, it establishes total transparency, trust, and accountability for self-help groups.

76
00:09:20,695 --> 00:09:23,873
Thank you for watching this project demonstration!
